dropped the body
--
N5008 [tuple.helper], [temp.spec.partial.match]/1, [temp.deduct.general]/8:
tuple_size<tuple<int, int>> selects the partial specialization for tuple<T...>
and has integral_constant<size_t, 2> as its base; the cv-qualified partial
specializations, guarded by `integral_constant<size_t, sizeof(tuple_size<T>)>'
inside an alias template argument, do not match a non-cv tuple.  Regression
test (round 163g): letting alias-template arguments skip the instantiation of
class template specializations they name (an attempted fix for
cpp11_alias_template_pointer_does_not_instantiate_pointee) completed
tuple_size<tuple<int, int>> WITHOUT its base, so `value' read nondet and
libc++'s std::apply returned void (cpp17_apply_basic/test_libcxx.desc).
Reduced by cvise from libc++ 18's <tuple> (/tmp/r163/red/reg_ts).
test_libcxx.desc checks the same with libc++.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18
accept both programs.
